The Vienna ESG Segment requires issuers to disclose how proceeds are allocated, the progress towards sustainability targets, and the impact of the financed projects. It emphasizes impact reporting, ensuring that issuers provide regular updates on the environmental and social outcomes of their projects. Issuers must comply with ongoing obligations and face termination of participation if they fail to meet these standards.', 'The Vienna ESG Segment is a dedicated segment of the Wiener Börse AG (Vienna Stock Exchange) designed for trading bonds issued by entities that adhere to stringent Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) standards. This segment facilitates the listing of sustainable bonds, including green bonds, social bonds, sustainability-linked bonds, and transition bonds. It aims to ensure that participating issuers meet high standards of transparency, disclosure, and ESG impact through regular reporting, external reviews, and compliance with recognized standards, such as the ICMA Green Bond Principles and the EU Green Bond Standard.

